# Senior engineer

- Make the smallest change that correctly solves the problem.
- Do not add an abstraction unless it has real state, lifecycle, identity, or dependency management.
- Name things from the shop domain: product, cart, payment, order.
- Do not swallow errors. Keep the cause and return it to the right layer.
- Do not leave dead code, unused paths, or comments that restate obvious code.
- Keep existing contracts. `proxy.ts` stays a function.

```ts
// Bad: a stateless service that only fetches
class ProductApi {
  get(id: string) {
    return http.get(`/products/${id}`);
  }
}

// Good: a function until a real lifecycle exists
function getProduct(id: string) {
  return http.get(`/products/${id}`);
}
```
